# Work-task file compliance

Applies when reading or editing files under `.general/tasks/`.

## Compliance check

### 1. Frontmatter (file top)

Minimum:

```yaml
---
work_task: v1
---
```

Sprint is **optional**. When the user (or file) has a sprint, include it:

```yaml
---
work_task: v1
sprint: 34
---
```

If `sprint` is set, visible meta must include `**Sprint:** <N>` matching frontmatter.

### 2. Filename

| Mode | Filename |
|------|----------|
| No sprint | `<TOPIC>.md` (e.g. `CUSTOMER_SERVICE_PAGES.md`) |
| Sprint `<N>` | `SPRINT_<N>_<TOPIC>.md` (e.g. `SPRINT_34_CUSTOMER_SERVICE_PAGES.md`) |

| Result | Agent action |
|--------|----------------|
| `work_task: v1`, no `sprint`, filename not `SPRINT_*` + required sections | Compliant (no-sprint). |
| `work_task: v1` + `sprint: <N>` + filename `SPRINT_<N>_*.md` + required sections | Compliant (sprint). |
| `sprint` set but filename not `SPRINT_<N>_*`, or filename `SPRINT_<N>_*` but `sprint` missing/mismatched | Fix meta and/or rename. Preserve content. Do not invent a sprint if neither side has one. |
| `work_task: skip` | Leave the file alone. |
| Missing, other value, or old `work_task` version | **Non-compliant.** Follow the **create-work-task** skill **Upgrade workflow**. |
| `*.plan.md` with Cursor plan frontmatter and no `work_task` | Prefer `work_task: skip` unless the user asks to convert it. |

## Required v1 sections (after frontmatter)

- `#` title + meta (`Status`, `Last updated`; `Sprint` only when sprint is set)
- `## Dashboard (daily self-check)` (+ `### Daily log`)
- `## Checkpoint (keep history; do not delete done rows)`
- `## Discuss (open questions)`

## Hard rules

- Preserve wording, checklists, links, and done/undone state from the old file.
- Do not invent Jira keys, progress, answers, or sprint numbers.
- Do not delete content; park leftovers under `## Legacy notes`.
- Do not ask for sprint on every create — only apply sprint naming/meta when the user provides it (or the file already has it).
- Creating a **new** task file also follows the **create-work-task** skill (Jira/Confluence optional; sprint optional).
